    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the acceptance test is the only test).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature. When a create request sets `sharesHousehold=true`, an owner sharing an existing same-lastName owner's address is allowed (already the case), and now every member of that household is assigned the same stable `householdId`, which is returned by the API.\n\n**Design** \u2014 the shared identifier is derived *deterministically* from the household's canonical (lastName, address) key, so any member computes the same value without cross-owner coordination. That logic lives in one small single-responsibility helper, reused by both the uniqueness check and the new assignment step.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`rest/function/owner/Household.java`** (new) \u2014 centralizes household identity: `key()`, `same()`, and a SHA-256-based `id()`. Case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed matching.\n- **`EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `Household.same(...)`, dropping its duplicated private `canonical()`.\n- **`rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerHousehold.java`** (new) \u2014 POST step that, only when `sharesHousehold=true`, sets the built owner's `householdId` and backfills the same id onto existing household members (so \"both\" owners share it). Governed by the create transaction.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHousehold` in after `build`, before `defaultRegistrationDate`.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with accessors.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added read-only `householdId` to the `Owner` response schema (MapStruct maps it by name; it's absent from `OwnerFields`, so it's never client-supplied).\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `household_id` column.",
